/*
CABIN IN THE WOODS — an AUTHORING template. The other templates help
you solve someone else's mystery; this one helps you write your own.

WHY THIS MANY ROOMS. A mystery is uncertainty about where people
were, so the map has to hold that uncertainty. One room: everyone is
together, every alibi is everyone's alibi — nothing to deduce. Two
rooms: a coin flip; the first clue ends it. The workable minimum is
about five or six places: enough that each suspect can CLAIM a
different one, that two suspects can vouch for each other while a
third stands unverified, and that sight lines and adjacency start
carrying clues ("she'd have seen him cross the main room", "he heard
the shed door from the clearing"). This cabin gives you four indoor
rooms, a porch, a clearing, the woods, and a shed — plus `unknown`,
the room for everyone the testimony hasn't accounted for yet.

HOW TO AUTHOR (write the truth first, then hide it):
  1. THE TRUTH — write everyone's REAL timeline: walks, the murder,
     the weapon's take/drop. You are the omniscient narrator here.
     Get it green against the victory checks you owe yourself
     (body where it's found, killer at the scene at time_of_death).
  2. THE TESTIMONY — one statement per suspect, written FROM the
     truth: the innocent tell it straight, the killer's claim
     contradicts it. The panel derives each claim's truth and
     assembles the liar certificate for you.
  3. THE CLUES — every clue you plan to give the reader becomes a
     check or goal HERE, against the true world. A clue that can't
     go red in any rival world discriminates nothing — delete it.
  4. THE AUDIT — your mystery is DONE when sole() binds exactly one
     answer, and BROKEN if it binds one before your last clue lands.
     Red-test: perturb the truth (move the killer, swap the weapon)
     and watch which gates catch it. The ones that don't are
     decoration.
*/

theme night
clock 9:00 minute(1)
time time_of_death 9:45
time discovered 10:10

// ---- the map ---------------------------------------------------------
room unknown size(8 2.5 5) at(-16 0 -14) color(black)

room main_room size(5 2.5 4) floor door(to porch) color(#6b5f4c)
room kitchen west-of(main_room) door(to main_room) size(3 2.5 4) floor color(#54685c)
room bunk_room east-of(main_room) door(to main_room) size(3 2.5 4) floor color(#5b586e)
room back_room north-of(main_room) door(to main_room) size(5 2.5 3) floor color(#6e5555) window(north 1 1 1)
// the window faces the woods: someone outside can see in — sight
// lines pass a window, bodies don't

room porch south-of(main_room) walls(0) size(5 2 2) color(#55503f)
room clearing south-of(porch) walls(0) size(12 2 5) color(#4d5742)
room woods west-of(clearing) size(5 2 12) walls(0) color(#3d4835)
room shed east-of(clearing) door(to clearing) size(2.5 2.2 2.5) color(#57503f)

part tree
  cylinder trunk r(0.14) h(1.4) color(#3a3028)
  sphere crown r(0.8) at(0 2 0) color(#22301f)
end
tree pine at(woods 0 0) repeat(4) spread(0.5 0 2.5) jitter(1.4 0 0.8 11)

// ---- the cast --------------------------------------------------------
//victim: found in ___ at ___
person body at(back_room 0.8 0.5) color(grey)
turn body to(90 0 0) over(0)

set suspects
person host at(unknown -3 -1) color(firebrick)
person cook at(unknown -2 -1) color(steelblue)
person guide at(unknown -1 -1) color(seagreen)
person stranger at(unknown 0 -1) color(darkgoldenrod)
end

box weapon size(0.35 0.1 0.1) at(unknown 2 1) color(#8a8d94)

// ---- 1. THE TRUTH (yours — the reader never sees this file) ----------
// the pattern, worked once: the cook really was in the kitchen 9:30
// to 9:50, and can say so
walk cook to(kitchen) over(0) start(9:30)
walk cook to(unknown -2 -1) over(0) start(9:50)
// ...write the killer's real path to the back_room here, the weapon's
// take/drop, and everyone else's true whereabouts. Return people to
// unknown when their real account ends — the amber lint below the
// panel will point at anyone left unaccounted.

// ---- 2. THE TESTIMONY ------------------------------------------------
// one per suspect, written FROM the truth; the killer's is the lie.
// The panel shows each claim's truth and derives the liar certificate.
statement cook present_at(cook, kitchen, 45)
// statement host ...
// statement guide ...
// statement stranger ...

// ---- 3. THE CLUES (each one gates the true world) --------------------
check always in(cook kitchen) during(9:30 9:50)
// check never sees(...)         — who could NOT have witnessed it
// check adjacent(shed clearing) — earwitness geometry
// check ever carries(...)       — who held the weapon, and when

// ---- 4. THE AUDIT ----------------------------------------------------
// where was everyone at the fatal moment?
?- set_member(suspects, X), where(X, time_of_death, R)
// who cannot be cleared for the scene?
?- could(suspects, X, back_room, time_of_death)
// the verdict — your mystery is finished when this binds EXACTLY one,
// and only after the final clue:
?- sole(suspects, X, back_room, time_of_death)
